     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Find $A^{-1}$ for $A=$ [[2, 1], [3, 4]] and solve $2x+y=5$, $3x+4y=10$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\text{det}\\, A=8-3=5$, so $A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{5}$ [[4, −1], [−3, 2]].",
      "$\\vec{x}=A^{-1}$ (5, 10) $=\\frac{1}{5}$ (20−10, −15+20) $=$ (2, 1). Check: $2(2)+1=5$, $3(2)+4(1)=10$."
     ],
     "answer": "$x=2$, $y=1$"
